  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fcf7219bab7fe46a1ad266029b2fee19, type: 3}
  m_Name: Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Readme
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  title: UI Prefabs
  sections:
  - heading: Naming conventions
    text: If everything follows naming conventions, it's great. <br>But most importantly,
      everything that has to be controlled by script should strictly adhere to these
      naming conventions. <br><br>Buttons should start with "B_" <br>Text (or labels)
      should start with "L_" (and not "T_" because they aren't textures) <br>Images
      (or sprites) should start with "I_" <br>Folders/Groups should start with G_
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Where to reference things
    text: Every prefab should have a custom UI Widget component at it's root, and
      as few other custom components as possible. <br><br>Every object that will
      get controlled by script must be referenced in this root component. <br><br>If
      the name for the gameObjects is strictly identical to that of the variable
      to which they must be assigned, they can be detected automatically by the script.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 0
